**Props**

| Prop | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `help` | `string \| Element` | No | None | Generates help text using this value as content. |
| `hideLabelFromVision` | `boolean` | No | None | When true, the label is visible only to screen readers. |
| `label` | `string` | No | None | Generates a label using this value as content. |
| `onChange` | `( value: string ) => void` | Yes | None | Receives the new textarea value each time it changes. |
| `rows` | `number` | No | `4` | Number of rows the textarea contains. |
| `value` | `string` | Yes | None | The current textarea value. |

Props not in this list are applied to the underlying textarea element.

**onChange signature:** `( value: string ) => void`

**Notes on `__nextHasNoMarginBottom` and deprecations:** The page doesn't mention `__nextHasNoMarginBottom` or any deprecations, so I can't provide details on them from this content.

**Usage example:**

```jsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { TextareaControl } from '@wordpress/components';

const MyTextareaControl = () => {
	const [ text, setText ] = useState( '' );

	return (
		<TextareaControl
			label="Text"
			help="Enter some text"
			value={ text }
			onChange={ ( value ) => setText( value ) }
		/>
	);
};
```

